---
description: Feature folders in Next.js apps — no cross-feature imports
globs: apps/*/src/**/*.{ts,tsx}
alwaysApply: false
---

# Feature modules

- `app/` and `src/proxy.ts` — composition roots. Import `@/features/<name>`.
- `features/<name>/` — one domain. Add `components/`, `hooks/`, `lib/`, `server/queries/`, `server/actions/` as needed. Relative imports inside the feature — not `@/features/<this-feature>/...`. Never import another feature.
- `shared/` — this app only; never import a feature.
- Cross-app libraries go in `packages/`.
- `src/lib` and `src/components` at the app root are not composition roots. Put that code in `shared/` or a feature.

## Names come from the ontology

`docs/product/ontology.md` holds the canonical domain terms. Those are the **only** names allowed — features, components, types, columns, routes, UI copy. A rejected synonym in the code is a defect, not a style preference. If the term you want is not there, the ontology is incomplete: say so rather than inventing a translation.

A `check-boundaries` failure means a mechanic has earned promotion to `shared/` or a package. It never means the rule should bend.
